<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>For schools, parents and staff</span>
      <span>Last updated 2 November 2026</span>
    </div>

    <p>
      The School Manager is school management software for Pakistani schools. This
      page covers the website (theschoolmanager.site), the software itself
      (app.theschoolmanager.site), the Windows program and the Android app. All
      four use the same records.
    </p>

    <h2>Whose records these are</h2>
    <p>
      A school uses the software to keep its own records. The school decides what
      is entered and who may see it, and we keep those records for the school. If
      you are a parent or a member of staff, the school that gave you your login is
      the place to ask about your information first; we will help it answer.
    </p>

    <h2>What is kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>About pupils:</b> name, father's name, date of birth, B-Form number,
        class, roll and GR numbers, a photo if the school adds one, attendance,
        marks and results, fees billed and paid, and certificates issued.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>About parents and guardians:</b> names, phone and WhatsApp numbers, a
        CNIC number if the school records one, and the family's login.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>About staff:</b> name, role, contact details, attendance and check-in
        times, and pay records.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Staff check-in:</b> where a school uses the check-in poster, the phone's
        camera reads its QR code (no picture is kept). If the school has also
        switched on its location check, the phone's location at that moment is sent
        once, to confirm the person is at school.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Logs:</b> who changed what and when, which phone or computer worked
        offline (an id the app makes for itself, the kind of device and the app's
        version), and when.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>The school's account with us:</b> its plan, invoices and payments.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What stays on a phone or computer</h2>
    <p>
      So that the software works without the internet, each phone or computer keeps
      a copy of what its login reads, and any work done offline until it has been
      sent. In the Android app this is in the app's own private storage, which no
      other app can read and which Android does not back up or copy to a new phone.
      The copies are removed when that login signs out. Work not yet sent stays
      until it has been sent, so nothing taken offline is lost.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The people the school gives a login to, each only what their role allows.</li>
      <li>A parent sees their own children, and nobody else's.</li>
      <li>
        When the school office gives a family or a teacher a password, its key ring
        keeps that password so the office can tell them again. Once they change it
        themselves, the key ring shows it is out of date.
      </li>
      <li>
        Our support team, only during a support visit, and every visit is listed
        for the school under Settings, Support visits.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Each school's records are kept apart from every other school's by the
      database itself, not only by the screens.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>
      There are no advertisements in the software or the apps, and nothing in them
      follows you to other websites or apps. We do not sell anybody's information,
      and we do not share it with anyone except the services that run the
      software, below.
    </p>

    <h2>The services that run it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Supabase</b> keeps the database and handles signing in, and stores
        passwords only in a form that cannot be read back. The servers are outside
        Pakistan.
      </li>
      <li><b>Cloudflare</b> serves the website and the software's files.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      They handle the records only to run the software. Everything travels over an
      encrypted connection.
    </p>

    <h2>The Android app's permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Internet and network state</b>, to send work and to know when the phone is offline.</li>
      <li><b>Camera</b>, only to read the check-in QR code, and only when you check in.</li>
      <li><b>Location</b>, only at check-in, and only if the school checks it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Choosing a photo uses Android's own picker, and printing uses Android's own
      print screen.
    </p>

    <h2>How long it is kept, and removing it</h2>
    <p>
      Records are kept while the school uses the software. A school can download a
      complete copy of its records at any time, including after it has stopped
      paying. When a school asks us to delete its records, we do, after it has had
      the chance to take that copy.
    </p>
    <p>
      Logins are made and switched off by the school. To have your login removed,
      or your information corrected or deleted, ask your school office. You can
      also write to us, and we will work with the school to do it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      The software holds pupils' records for their school. Pupils do not sign in:
      the apps are for school staff and for parents.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or about your information:
      <a class="clink" id="contact-email" hidden href="#"></a>
      or <a href="/contact">the contact page</a>. If this policy changes, this page
      says so, with the date.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
